details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The two plates are centered in the frame, one sharp in the immediate foreground and the second slightly blurred in the background. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view, capturing the full volume of the scramble. The lighting is soft natural side light from a window to the left, creating gentle, realistic shadows and highlighting the texture of the eggs. The surface is a worn, dark wooden table with visible grain and a light dusting of stray cumin spice. Each matte ceramic plate contains a generous, fluffy mound of soft, yellow-and-white egg scramble, interspersed with tender, golden-brown diced sweet potatoes and dark, firm black beans. The scramble is not a solid block but has a loose, folded, and pillowy texture. Bright red chunky salsa is pooled in small, rustic dollops on top of the eggs, with vibrant green, creamy cubes of avocado nestled alongside. Fresh, hand-chopped cilantro leaves are scattered unevenly over the top. A wooden spatula rests casually on the table next to the plates. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: a small salsa drip on the plate rim, asymmetric avocado placement, and uneven browning on the sweet potatoes. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few stray cilantro leaves on the table and a slight oil mark near the plate. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature—cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
